     "type": "message",
     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, and your confirmation doesn't change that.\n\n- **You aren't the prescriber.** Confirming the order as written doesn't make it a clinical decision. The prescriber responsible for the patient has to make that decision.\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 5,100 mg per day is about twice the maximum labeled daily dose. Nothing in the patient details you gave, such as normal kidney and liver function, supports going that high.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the treating physician or another authorized prescriber to review the order. If the dose was a typo, they can correct it.\n- If they do want a dose above the usual maximum, they should enter it themselves. Pharmacy will probably review it before it's dispensed.\n\nIf the prescriber sends me a corrected dose, or a documented rationale for this one, I can enter it then."
      }
     ],
